## MAJ findings

### R5-COR-MAJ-001 (correctness): missing unmodified-log negative test for onboarded-operator-bump

**Bug:** test harness has the unmodified-log error case for `cascade-status: onboarded` (line 226) but NO equivalent for `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump`. The first guard in the operator-bump check path (`branch_log_modified == 0` → die) is permanently untested in its failure direction.

**Fix:** in tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh, add a test case: init_case_repo, write DISPATCH-NOTE with `cascade-status: onboarded-operator-bump` + valid Target line, write STATUS.md with regex-passing TF row, do NOT modify branch-protection-log.md (leave it empty), commit_case, run_case expecting exit 1 + diagnostic 'ERROR: branch-protection-log.md was not modified for cascade-status=onboarded-operator-bump'. Place adjacent to existing onboarded-operator-bump positive cases for clear test-matrix coverage.

### R5-COR-MAJ-002 (correctness): test_scaffold_downstream.sh leaks tmpdirs on failure

**Bug:** `make_output_dir()` creates `out.XXXXXX` directories directly under `REPO_ROOT`; the EXIT trap only removes `$TMPDIR`, so leaked artifacts accumulate on test failure and have no .gitignore coverage.

**Fix:** in tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh, change `make_output_dir` to create under `$TMPDIR`: `mktemp -d "${TMPDIR}/out.XXXXXX"`. The EXIT trap already cleans $TMPDIR. Verify all subsequent uses of make_output_dir's return value still resolve correctly (relative paths inside TMPDIR; absolute paths if REPO_ROOT-cd'd previously).

### R5-COR-MAJ-003 (correctness): missing test for non-HEAD-SHA warn path

**Bug:** plan-doc spec for scaffold-downstream.sh says 'warns when SHA is not main HEAD but continues'. test_scaffold_downstream.sh has all happy-path invocations using `rev-parse HEAD`, guaranteeing SHA == main HEAD; the non-HEAD warn path is never exercised.

**Fix:** in tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh, add a test case: obtain `git rev-parse HEAD^` (parent of HEAD), invoke scaffold-downstream.sh with that SHA, assert exit 0 + stderr contains 'is not current SCP main HEAD' + all 4 output files present. If HEAD^ doesn't exist (fresh repo edge case), use any other valid commit SHA from the repo log.

### SAFE-MAJ-001 (safety_bypass): system-path deny list bypassable via path traversal

**Bug:** scaffold-downstream.sh system-path deny list (lines 131-135 region) uses raw string case-pattern matching. An --output-dir value like `/Users/amplience/Projects/standards-control-plane/../../../etc` passes the case match (doesn't start with /etc) but resolves via OS to /etc.

**Fix:** in scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh, BEFORE the system-path case check, normalise: `OUTPUT_DIR="$(readlink -f "$OUTPUT_DIR" 2>/dev/null || printf '%s' "$OUTPUT_DIR")"`. Note macOS `readlink` predates `-f` on some versions; use python3 fallback if needed: `python3 -c "import os,sys; print(os.path.realpath(sys.argv[1]))" "$OUTPUT_DIR"`. Add a test case in tests/scaffolder/test_scaffold_downstream.sh: `--output-dir "$(mktemp -d "$TMPDIR/tr.XXXXXX")/../../etc"` expecting exit 1.

### SAFE-MAJ-002 (safety_bypass): ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 dependency on Gate 2 still advisory

**Bug:** fix-round-2's MAJ-BYPASS-006 closure added a Gate 3 prerequisite check, but the language is 'If you want the helper to enforce...' — leaving the `--expected-wrapper-sha` flag optional. This is advisory not mechanical.

**Fix:** in docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.8 Gate 3:
1. Change the `--expected-wrapper-sha` language from 'If you want the helper to enforce...' to: 'REQUIRED: pass `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-gate-2>` — do NOT re-enable without it. Gate 3 without --expected-wrapper-sha leaves the cascade re-armed against an unverified wrapper SHA, defeating the break-glass safety chain.'
2. Reorder so the --expected-wrapper-sha bullet is the FIRST step of Gate 3, not buried under the 'Verify Gate 2 completion' subsection.
3. In scripts/enable-required-check.sh, when `--restore` was previously invoked on a target (detected by checking if the prior log entry exists in branch-protection-log.md for that target), enforce that subsequent forward-mode invocation requires `--expected-wrapper-sha` OR explicit `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` override. Document the new flag in --help + ADOPT-001 §12.8.

### MAJ-CG-001 (completeness): ADOPT-001 §12.7.1 wrapper filename mismatch

**Bug:** ADOPT-001 §12.7.1 documents wrapper filename as `policy-check.yml`, but scaffolder emits `policy-check-wrapper.yml` and forward-mode safety check (post-fix-round-3) hardcodes that path. Manual adopters following §12.7 land on the wrong filename and fail the safety check.

**Fix:** in docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.7.1, add a callout: 'Cascade-onboarded adopters get `policy-check-wrapper.yml` (emitted by scaffold-downstream.sh per WP-SCP-024). Pre-cascade manual adopters using §12.7 may have used `policy-check.yml`; cascade rollout via 024C+ standardises on `policy-check-wrapper.yml` as the canonical adopter wrapper filename. The forward-mode safety check in `enable-required-check.sh` looks for the canonical path; manual adopters with the older filename should rename to the canonical filename before invoking enable-required-check.sh, or pass `--wrapper-path .github/workflows/<their-name>.yml` (TBD: not currently implemented; tracked as TF-024B-003 for follow-on).'

Add TF-024B-003 to STATUS.md tracked-forward items: '- **TF-024B-003** (open): scripts/enable-required-check.sh forward-mode safety check hardcodes `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`; add `--wrapper-path` flag for manual adopters using the older policy-check.yml naming; non-blocking for cohort cascade (which uses scaffolder + canonical filename) but should close before pre-cascade manual adopters interact with enable-required-check.sh.'

### MAJ-CG-002 (completeness): VERSIONING.md missing new flags

**Bug:** VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper protected flag list omits three flags added in this slice: `--expected-wrapper-sha`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`.

**Fix:** in policies/VERSIONING.md, locate the §Branch-protection helper protected flag list (the existing 7-flag entry from prior slices) and add the three new flags maintaining the existing format. Adding flags is additive — no semver bump required.

### MAJ-CG-003 (completeness): pending --restore demo tracking

**Bug:** the pending --restore real-repo round-trip demo is tracked in 3 places (DISPATCH-NOTE checkbox, STATUS.md prose, R3 fix-round-2 added TF-024B-002 to STATUS.md). Reviewer wants cleaner consolidation.

**Fix:** verify TF-024B-002 in STATUS.md is the canonical tracking entry (added in fix-round-3); add a one-line cross-reference in DISPATCH-NOTE Acceptance criteria that points at TF-024B-002 instead of duplicating prose. Format: `[ ] (operator step 7; tracked at TF-024B-002 in STATUS.md) --restore round-trip via captured before-state...`. STATUS.md outcome row text can stay prose — the TF row is the canonical resume surface.

