{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":593237,\"duration_api_ms\":593809,\"num_turns\":13,\"result\":\"{\\\"review_summary\\\":\\\"Slice 024B delivers all plan-doc §6 scope items: scaffolder, adopter-wrapper template, --restore mode, check-invocation-log-entry.sh covering all 4 CI behaviours, tests, ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass, and D-044. No plan-doc invariants are violated. Anti-descoping check passes: every item in the §6 024B row is accounted for. D-044 reservation is honoured — the filed decision matches the reserved topic exactly, covering all 4 components. FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 is correctly named in DISPATCH-NOTE §Cohort cascade gate and STATUS.md 024B outcome as a 024C-F gate. All 6 DISPATCH-NOTE worked-example matrix cases are tested in the check-invocation-log-entry.sh test harness. CASCADE-PR-BODY.md template covers invariants 1, 3, 5, 9 explicitly. ADOPT-001 §12.8 is correctly placed between §12.7.15 and §13; §12.7 Reference gains D-044; §12.8 Reference includes D-044, WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, and ADOPT-001 §12.7. ACC notifications dir is correctly scoped out. No FLA references appear as preconditions. Three MAJ findings impede clean closure: §12.7.1 file-name divergence creates an inconsistent operator path; three 024B-added flags are absent from VERSIONING.md protected list; the --restore round-trip demo lacks a formal TF entry. Two MIN gaps around SLO qualification and cross-repo FUP traceability. Two nit items on sequencing table staleness.\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MAJ-CG-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"ADOPT-001 §12.7.1 documents the wrapper filename as policy-check.yml, but the scaffolder emits policy-check-wrapper.yml and enable-required-check.sh forward-mode safety check hardcodes that path. Manual adopters following §12.7 fail the safety check.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"scaffold-downstream.sh:152 sets wrapper_path to policy-check-wrapper.yml. enable-required-check.sh:276-280 selects .path==\\\\\\\".github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml\\\\\\\". ADOPT-001 §12.7.1: 'Add this file at .github/workflows/policy-check.yml in your repo.' §12.7.3 says to run enable-required-check.sh without distinguishing paths.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Pre-cascade adopters following §12.7.1→§12.7.3 fail the safety check with 'no workflow at policy-check-wrapper.yml'. Error message hints at cascade path but §12.7 presents a single unified onboarding flow. Workaround exists (--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci) but is undiscoverable from §12.7 prose.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add a callout in ADOPT-001 §12.7.1 distinguishing cascade path (scaffolder→policy-check-wrapper.yml) from pre-cascade manual path (policy-check.yml). Alternatively, make enable-required-check.sh forward-mode check accept either filename, or add a note to the error message for manual adopters.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MAJ-CG-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper protected flag list omits three flags added in this slice: --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement, --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks. ADOPT-001 §12.8 documents all three as part of the break-glass procedure.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"VERSIONING.md lines 91-92 list 7 protected flags, all pre-024B. enable-required-check.sh adds these 3 at lines 193-197. ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 1 references both --i-understand-restore-removes-* flags. §12.8 Gate 3 references --expected-wrapper-sha. None appear in VERSIONING.md protected list.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Future removal of any of these three flags without a MAJOR version bump would silently break the documented §12.8 break-glass procedure for all cascade adopters. The governance contract (documented in §12.8 as operator-facing procedure) diverges from the versioning contract (VERSIONING.md as the breaking-change authority).\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add --expected-wrapper-sha, --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement, and --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks to VERSIONING.md §Branch-protection helper protected flag list, mirroring the pre-existing 7-flag entry.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MAJ-CG-003\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MAJ\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"The pending --restore real-repo round-trip demo (operator step 7) is tracked as an unchecked AC checkbox in DISPATCH-NOTE and prose in STATUS.md, but has no formal TF entry in STATUS.md tracked-forward items. This is a hard-prerequisite for 024C merge per plan-doc §6 and §10 Q3.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §Acceptance criteria: '[ ] (operator step 7) --restore round-trip ... on a real throw-away test repo'. STATUS.md 024B row: 'evidence PENDING — operator-interactive demo at step 7'. No TF-024B-RESTORE-ROUNDTRIP-EVIDENCE row in STATUS.md tracked-forward sections. Plan-doc §10 Q3: 'closes only when 024B acceptance criterion in §6 is met'.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Without a formal TF, the pending demo cannot be systematically tracked across sessions. A future session resuming from STATUS.md alone cannot identify this as a 024C-blocking open item without reading the DISPATCH-NOTE AC section. Completeness governance invariant requires named tracked-forward items.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add TF-024B-RESTORE-ROUNDTRIP-EVIDENCE to STATUS.md tracked-forward items with: status (open), 024C-precondition note, and path docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md. Reference from DISPATCH-NOTE §Acceptance criteria.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MIN-CG-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 is named as a 024C-F gate in DISPATCH-NOTE §Cohort cascade gate and STATUS.md 024B outcome prose, but has no dedicated STATUS.md TF row for cross-session traceability.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §Cohort cascade gate: '024C entry is conditional on FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure'. STATUS.md 024B row mentions it in the outcome field prose. STATUS.md tracked-forward items sections contain no TF row for this item. Plan-doc §6 amendment also names it as precondition.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"A cross-repo dependency blocking 4 cohort slices (024C-F) with no STATUS.md TF entry creates a session-continuity risk. Future sessions must re-derive the precondition from DISPATCH-NOTE prose rather than STATUS.md tracked items index.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Add to STATUS.md tracked-forward items: 'TF-024-FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 (open): ACC-side per-repo dispatcher install pattern; gates 024C-F cohort cascade; ACC repo is the resolution target.'\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"MIN-CG-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"MIN\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 1 states 'SLO: <30 min from operator decision to restored state' unconditionally, but plan-doc invariant 7 explicitly marks this SLO as aspirational until the step-7 real-repo round-trip demo completes.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 1: 'SLO: <30 min from operator decision to restored state.' Plan-doc §2 invariant 7: 'claimed only after slice 024B closes with a demonstrated real-repo round-trip (not a dry-run mock).' DISPATCH-NOTE AC step 7 checkbox is unchecked. STATUS.md confirms demo is PENDING.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Adopters reading §12.8 pre-merge see an SLO claim the plan-doc explicitly defers. If the real-repo demo reveals the SLO is not achievable in 30 min (e.g., API rate limits, PAT scope delays), §12.8 would require retroactive correction post-merge with no currently-planned review cycle to catch the drift.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Amend §12.8 Gate 1 to: 'SLO: <30 min from operator decision to restored state (demonstrated at slice 024B step 7; evidence at docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md).' Update phrasing once evidence is committed.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nit-CG-001\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"Sequencing table Phase 5 shows '🔄 variable; expect 1–3 rounds' without reflecting that 3 fix-rounds are already complete per git log. The estimate and status are stale.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE Sequencing table Phase 5 status: '🔄'. Git log: 'fix-round-3: 1 CRIT + 6 MAJ closed', 'fix-round-2: 1 CRIT + 7 MAJ closed', 'fix-round-1: 2 CRIT + 9 MAJ + MIN/nit batch closed'. Current pass (this review) is R4.\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Stale sequencing table reduces at-a-glance traceability for reviewers determining current fix-round state from DISPATCH-NOTE. Minor.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Update Phase 5 status to '🔄 3 rounds complete; R4 in progress' and reflect actual wall-clock elapsed time rather than the original 'variable' estimate.\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"nit-CG-002\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"nit\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE status line at the bottom reads 'v0.2 — implementation complete; fix-rounds underway' but does not reflect that 3 fix-rounds are complete and R4 is now in progress.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"DISPATCH-NOTE final line: 'Status: v0.2 — implementation complete; fix-rounds underway; pending operator step 7 --restore demo and self-merge.' Git log shows 3 fix-round commits: fix-round-1 (2 CRIT + 9 MAJ), fix-round-2 (1 CRIT + 7 MAJ), fix-round-3 (1 CRIT + 6 MAJ).\\\",\\\"impact\\\":\\\"Version staleness makes it harder for future session operators to determine the current R-pass count from the DISPATCH-NOTE version line alone. Minor.\\\",\\\"mitigation\\\":\\\"Bump DISPATCH-NOTE status to 'v0.3 — fix-rounds 1-3 complete; R4 underway; pending step 7 operator demo and self-merge' before committing the next fix-round.\\\"}]}\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"becabf00-2f84-4414-8d57-9b90e97e6d7c\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0779658,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":5632,\"cache_creation_in