en a second maintainer arrives. Forward-looking discipline preserved: when a second maintainer onboards, flip count=1 + codeowner=true + non-author=true in one operation. Both corrections are landed in `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent re-run reproduces the live state) + `docs/security/branch-protection.md` + WP-SCP-020 §8 risk row. The 2026-07-21 quarterly escalation review re-evaluates the personal-account shape | ACCEPTED | First-PR-through-enforcement is the operational test of the spec; the test surfaced two assumptions that didn't survive contact with GitHub's actual behaviour: (1) the bare context name from 020B(xi) was incomplete (didn't anticipate Actions' `<workflow> / <job>` rendering for reusable-workflow callers), and (2) \"self-approval is the only option\" in 020K's wording was operationally impossible (GitHub forbids PR self-review). Both corrections are operational closure of the spec gap; neither weakens the security posture. The 4-layer protection (signed commits + required check + no admin bypass + tag protection) remains intact. The review-count=0 acceptance is the explicit bus-factor-1 cost; review enforcement returns the moment a second maintainer joins. Identified by USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64's failed merge attempt 2026-04-30 |\n| D-034 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020F renovate-tag-protection (parallel ruleset to D-030's `v*` ruleset, targeting `refs/tags/renovate/v*`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001: `renovate/v*` tag series unprotected — an attacker with push access could silently re-point `renovate/v1.0.0` to a malicious commit and cascade adversarial Renovate config to every estate adopter on their next scheduled run. The 020J ruleset matches `refs/tags/v*` (literal v-prefix at start) only. New ruleset `scp-tag-protection-renovate-v` applies same protections (deletion / non_fast_forward / update blocked, `enforcement: active`, `bypass_actors: []`). Configured via `scripts/configure-020f-renovate-tag-protection.sh` (idempotent, jq-based JSON construction to eliminate heredoc-interpolation injection surface, multi-property post-creation verification). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md` \"Tag protection — renovate/v* pattern\" section. Symmetric with D-030 in posture and rationale; the only material difference is the tag-pattern segment. The `renovate/v*` series carries equal supply-chain weight as `v*` because every adopter that extends the preset cascades changes from the renovate-pattern tag to their own gate config | ACCEPTED | The 020J ruleset's `v*` literal-prefix pattern is by-design narrow; broadening to all release-track tags would require a separate ruleset per pattern. Renovate's preset shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-//renovate/default#renovate/v1.0.0` is the standard Renovate adopter onboarding shape; without ruleset protection, the entire preset trust chain is rooted in mutable tag refs. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged identically to D-030: the same admin who owns @jrnb2024 is the one publishing tags; the protection guards against accidental force-push, not against malicious admin action. Quarterly review cadence (2026-07-30 in STATUS.md \"Open scheduled follow-ups\") covers both rulesets together. Identified by 020F R1 safety review (workflow run dispatched 2026-04-30 evening) — surfaced under the no-silent-descope governance invariant after fix-round-1 closed the substantive R1 findings |\n| D-035 | 2026-04-30 | Adopt the WP-SCP-020 slice 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine. The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The `required_pull_request_reviews` preservation reflects that adopters with multi-maintainer teams have legitimate review-shape state that 020G must not destroy. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + 020G R1 review (3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 2 nit on safety, 2 MAJ + 4 MIN + nit on completeness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\n| D-036 | 2026-05-01 | Adopt `policies/VERSIONING.md` MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH semver contract on the SCP federation primitive's public surfaces (`workflow_call.inputs` on `policy-check.yml`, `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` + `schemas/rule-config.schema.json`, `SCP-R-NNN` rule IDs) WITH a one-release deprecation ramp before any breaking change AND `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/` RFC-lite process (quorum=1 SCP-CODEOWNER per D-031 single-operator mode; 48h wall-clock window with weekend-counts; 0 approvals = auto-defer with `defer` label; bypass-introducing proposals require explicit §5 enumeration and a non-waivable 48h window per 020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure) as estate doctrine for SCP federation primitive versioning and rule governance. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5. Forward-compat to 2-of-N quorum when a second maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation path, 2026-07-21 review). Internal-only surfaces (`lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`, `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`, helper scripts in `scripts/`, Renovate preset internal shape, OPA Rego helpers in `policies/scp_common.rego`) are explicitly NOT covered — they may be refactored without notice | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation): every new governance procedure binding adopter behaviour ships a ratifying D-NNN row to make the doctrine searchable in the canonical decision-record home rather than buried in a slice DISPATCH-NOTE. The one-release deprecation ramp is the MINIMUM version-skew adopters must tolerate before a surface vanishes; combined with the Renovate preset's automated SHA-pin bumps, this gives every adopter at least one full PR cycle's worth of warning annotations before a breaking change lands. The RFC-lite process is intentionally lightweight at v1.0.0 because the SCP estate is single-operator; the auto-defer mechanism is currently a manual close + label step. As estate scale grows (WP-SCP-024 cascade), the auto-defer mechanism may be lifted to a GitHub Action that runs on