{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"TF-024B-002|TF-024B-003|Tracked-forward items from 024B|TF-024X-renovate|D-044\" STATUS.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md policies/VERSIONING.md docs/DECISIONS.md'","aggregated_output":"docs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-09 (D-044 filed at WP-SCP-024 024B; D-045 / D-046 remain reserved; estate cascade)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 is reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:43:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B operational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; future wrapper-shape changes land in the template + propagate via Renovate SHA bumps. (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state, validates the captured GET-shape JSON, transforms it into the PUT payload by stripping `_links` / `url` / `checks` envelope fields, flattening `enforce_admins.enabled` back to a boolean, preserving `required_pull_request_reviews` recursively, and normalising invalid or absent `restrictions` to null. Restore mode now warns and requires explicit acknowledgements when the captured pre-state would remove `enforce_admins` or clear `required_status_checks.contexts`, captures the observed current branch-protection state immediately before PUT, and mirrors forward-mode's APPLY_FAIL pattern so failed PUTs still emit an audit log before exiting non-zero. New safety check (forward mode only): resolves the canonical wrapper by repo-relative path (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) instead of workflow display name, then refuses to invoke unless the repo has at least one successful `policy-check` workflow run in the last 60 days on the target branch; optional `--expected-wrapper-sha` lets the operator verify the adopter wrapper pin matches the Gate 2 release SHA before re-arming. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Slug matching canonicalises adopter names to lowercased hyphen-only owner/repo strings so dots/underscores collapse to hyphens before regex matching. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:7:**Decision filed:** D-044 (scaffolder operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension + `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:34:| Invocation-log CI enforcer | `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` | Implements plan-doc invariant 2's 4 CI behaviours: (a) **fail-closed default** for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; (b) `onboarded` → log entry present + target match; (c) `onboarded-operator-bump` → log entry present + target match + STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex format spec literally; (d) `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` → DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex spec literally + log file NOT modified in PR diff. Regex literal: `TF-024X-(renovate\\|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open\\|pending\\|in-progress\\|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:36:| `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo | `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` | NOT a dry-run mock per plan-doc invariant 7 SLO honesty + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003. Throw-away test repo (e.g. `jrnb2024/scp-024b-restore-test`); capture before-state via existing log entry shape; mutate branch protection; restore via `--restore`; verify byte-for-byte match. Evidence captured for D-044 ratification. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:39:| D-044 filing | `docs/DECISIONS.md` row | Scaffolder operational contract + adopter-template versioning + invocation-log convention extension + `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode semantics. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:64:| `- **TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim** (open): Renovate disabled on PIM; operator-bumped @abc123 at 024C; track until adopter enables Renovate cohort.` | ✅ | STATUS.md bullet wrapping passes; regex doesn't care about wrapper |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:66:| `- **TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim**` | ❌ | no status field |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:67:| `- **TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim** (open):` | ❌ | empty description (0 chars after `: `) |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:68:| `- **TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim** (open):                    ` | ❌ | all-whitespace description fails `\\S` anchor |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:69:| `- **TF-024X-renovate-jrnb2024-pim** (open): short` | ❌ | only 5 chars after `: `, fails `.{19,}` |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:80:  - [ ] `onboarded-operator-bump`: requires log entry + target match + STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:82:- [ ] D-044 filed.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:119:2. **Codex Tier 3 executor** (direct `codex exec --model gpt-5.4-mini` with reasoning-effort medium) — implementation: scaffolder + template + `--restore` extension + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + tests + ADOPT-001 §12 break-glass + D-044 row + STATUS.md update. Capture work-package + stdout to `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/codex-dispatch-manual-audit.log`.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:133:| 2 | Codex executor (direct `codex exec`): scaffolder + template + `--restore` + CI script + unit tests + ADOPT-001 §12 + D-044 row + STATUS.md | Codex T3 deviated | ~45–60 min | ✅ |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:148:Per `docs/DECISIONS.md` header, D-044 is reserved for this slice. Codex executor MUST NOT assign D-044 to any other decision filed during this slice. The reservation pattern mirrors D-021 (WP-SCP-022) + D-041–043 (WP-SCP-023) + D-044/045/046 (WP-SCP-024 reservation block already in place).\nSTATUS.md:3:**Last updated:** 2026-05-09 (WP-SCP-024 024B - scaffolder + --restore + invocation-log CI; D-044 filed; previous: 2026-05-09 D-035-rules retired)\nSTATUS.md:119:| 6 | #102 | **024A** | WP-SCP-024 plan-doc v0.1 — estate cascade. Defines adopter cohort `{pim, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower}` (per D-035) explicitly **FLA-independent** per operator direction; canary-first sequencing PIM → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:137:**Slice 024B remains the immediate work** — hard predecessor for cohort onboarding 024C-F per WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §6. Scope unchanged: scaffolder + `--restore` mode + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` + D-044 + real-repo rollback round-trip.\nSTATUS.md:143:| 1 | #<scaffolder-PR> | **024B** | D-044 filed; protocol deviation noted (direct codex exec for 024B; cohort cascade 024C-F gated on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure); plan-doc §6 amended with cohort dispatcher precondition; ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure shipped; scaffolder + template + `--restore` + invocation-log CI + tests all live; `--restore` real-repo round-trip evidence PENDING — operator-interactive demo at step 7 of dispatch plan; evidence path `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` to be committed post-demo, pre-merge, per plan-doc §6 acceptance criterion. |\nSTATUS.md:252:## Tracked-forward items from 024B\nSTATUS.md:255:- **TF-024B-002** (open): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md) — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7; merge-blocking AC per plan-doc §6 + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003; closes when operator runs forward-mode + --restore round-trip on throw-away test repo + commits byte-for-byte match evidence.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
