{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"branch-protection-log|Invocation log entry|restore pre-state|expected-wrapper-sha|prior log\" scripts/enable-required-check.sh docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/DECISIONS.md STATUS.md'","aggregated_output":"STATUS.md:266:- **D-035 (2026-04-30)** — 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` two-call PUT + POST shape, refuses CI, preserves `required_pull_request_reviews`, mandatory invocation-log commit at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`.\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:32:#     `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` and merge.\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:158:  --expected-wrapper-sha SHA\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:194:    --expected-wrapper-sha)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:195:      [ $# -lt 2 ] && { echo \"error: --expected-wrapper-sha requires a value\" >&2; usage; exit 2; }\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:421:        print(\"[020G] WARNING: restore pre-state restrictions contained unexpected fields: {}; restoring users/teams/apps only\".format(\", \".join(unexpected)), file=sys.stderr)\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:474:      echo \"[020G] WARNING: restore pre-state would remove admin enforcement (enforce_admins.enabled=false)\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:477:      echo \"[020G] WARNING: restore pre-state would clear required status checks (required_status_checks.contexts empty or null)\" >&2\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:510:## Invocation log entry\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:512:Append the block below to docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md on the SCP repo, commit on a feature branch, open PR, merge:\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:739:LOG_FILE=\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\"\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:749:## Invocation log entry\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:861:7. Emits an invocation-log markdown block for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` on the SCP repo. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1195:1. **Gate 1 (DISABLE):** run `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <captured-pre-state.json>` to restore the target adopter's branch protection from the captured `before` state in the original invocation log entry. The pre-state JSON lives at the bottom of every invocation log block in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; copy it to a local file first before invoking the restore mode.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1205:      If you want the helper to enforce that comparison for you, pass `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-gate-2>` to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch>`.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:82:| D-035 | 2026-04-30 | Adopt the WP-SCP-020 slice 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine. The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check` traces to D-033 (the rendered Actions check-run name established for the SCP self-dogfood gate). Adopters of the SCP federation primitive enable this required status check on their default branch via `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` from the SCP repo. The script applies branch protection in two API calls (unified PUT for status-checks/admins/reviews + dedicated POST to `required_signatures` sub-resource per the GitHub API shape), refuses to bypass admin enforcement without an explicit `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` acknowledgement flag, refuses to run in CI (CI=true / GITHUB_ACTIONS=true env-var guards), preserves any pre-existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it, and emits an invocation-log block (operator, timestamp, script SHA256 + git SHA, target repo+branch, before/after API JSON) for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure: an apply without the log entry is considered unrecorded. Estate cascade rollout (WP-SCP-024) drives this script across PIM, recommender, shopify-app, mapp-doc-agent, control-tower; FLA pilot (WP-SCP-020.1) is the canary first invocation | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection), D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account), D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-status-check), D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection): every operational procedure that mutates third-party repository state ships an idempotent applier + ratifying D-NNN + invocation log convention. The bootstrap-only / no-CI guard reflects that this script writes to a third-party repo's branch protection — an automation tool that ran it unattended could mass-mutate the estate via stolen credentials before any operator noticed. The `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` confirmation reflects that `--no-enforce-admins` defeats the whole point of the federation primitive on the target repo and so should require explicit intent. The `required_pull_request_reviews` preservation reflects that adopters with multi-maintainer teams have legitimate review-shape state that 020G must not destroy. Identified at WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + 020G R1 review (3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 2 nit on safety, 2 MAJ + 4 MIN + nit on completeness, 3 MAJ + 2 MIN + 2 nit on correctness — fixpoint via fix-round-1) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:90:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B operational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; future wrapper-shape changes land in the template + propagate via Renovate SHA bumps. (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state, validates the captured GET-shape JSON, transforms it into the PUT payload by stripping `_links` / `url` / `checks` envelope fields, flattening `enforce_admins.enabled` back to a boolean, preserving `required_pull_request_reviews` recursively, and normalising invalid or absent `restrictions` to null. Restore mode now warns and requires explicit acknowledgements when the captured pre-state would remove `enforce_admins` or clear `required_status_checks.contexts`, captures the observed current branch-protection state immediately before PUT, and mirrors forward-mode's APPLY_FAIL pattern so failed PUTs still emit an audit log before exiting non-zero. New safety check (forward mode only): resolves the canonical wrapper by repo-relative path (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) instead of workflow display name, then refuses to invoke unless the repo has at least one successful `policy-check` workflow run in the last 60 days on the target branch; optional `--expected-wrapper-sha` lets the operator verify the adopter wrapper pin matches the Gate 2 release SHA before re-arming. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Slug matching canonicalises adopter names to lowercased hyphen-only owner/repo strings so dots/underscores collapse to hyphens before regex matching. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
