ery other shape of the 48h window unchanged: bypass-introducing proposals keep the non-waivable minimum (the threat-surface justifies the wait); the post-2nd-maintainer-onboard 48h becomes mandatory minimum so the second maintainer has time to review; the 48h CEILING for auto-defer remains so abandoned proposals are surfaced. Symmetric with D-033's \"operational reality must amend the spec when the spec encounters a constraint that wasn't anticipated\" pattern. Identified at WP-SCP-022 slice 020L post-R2 fixpoint by operator (`@jrnb2024`) when reviewing the merge-readiness of PR #89 |\n| D-041 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B (this PR). The schema defines aggregated per-rule counts (raw_findings, denies, waived, rule_config_disabled), waivers aggregate (active_count, by_rule_id, expiring_within_30d), rule-config aggregate (disabled_rules, expiring_within_30d), repo / ref / commit / scp_version / RFC3339 emitted_at, and a verdict (allow/deny/warn). The schema EXPLICITLY DOES NOT include waiver content (`reason`, `approved_by`, `waiver_id` strings) — invariant 2 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc binds this. The reusable workflow gains a `scorecard-emit: bool` `workflow_call` input (default false) so existing adopters see no behaviour change; opt-in adopters set `with: scorecard-emit: true`. Schema versioning: MAJOR-pinned per `policies/VERSIONING.md` D-036 + WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1 — aggregator drops emits with unknown `schema_version`. Verification: GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation (OIDC-based) via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0` (SHA `a2bbfa25...`) at emit time; aggregator verifies via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` (per D-042 to be filed at slice 023C). v1.2.0 cut on this slice's merge per VERSIONING.md MINOR category | ACCEPTED | This is the first slice of WP-SCP-023's implementation chain (023A plan-doc landed at PR #97, commit `7075234`, 2026-05-03 R4 fixpoint). The data shape was specified at plan-doc level; this slice ratifies it as code surface. Default-false on the workflow input is the load-bearing safety property: existing adopters cannot have new behaviour spring on them; opt-in is explicit per invariant 4. The waiver-content exclusion (invariant 2) is enforced by the schema's `additionalProperties: false` constraint on every level + the explicit field enumeration. The MAJOR-pinning posture means schema breakage requires v2.0.0 + adopter migration; v0.1 prefix on `schema_version` reflects the freedom to amend until first adopter opts in. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation |\n| D-042 | 2026-05-03 | Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C (this PR). Mechanism: per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (the GitHub Actions Artifact Attestation OIDC pattern, mandatory per the D-042 reservation note above + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits (slice 020J) + `output/scorecards/** @jrnb2024` CODEOWNERS coverage (slice 023A) + branch protection on main (slice 020D2), NOT a separate Ed25519 key layer. The aggregator runs as `.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml` on a weekly cron (Monday 06:00 UTC) + `workflow_dispatch`; two-job structure (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped via job-level permissions, mirroring the 023B `attest-scorecard` job split); reads `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` (CODEOWNERS-protected at `docs/scorecards/**`), pulls each adopter's latest green policy-check run's `scorecard-emit.json` artifact, verifies attestation, schema-validates emit, aggregates into `output/scorecards/index.json` (schema: `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`), and opens a PR for operator review. Failure modes (verification_failure / unreachable / no_emit) record loudly per-adopter — never silently dropped. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema `additionalProperties: false` at every level). Internal-only workflow per `policies/VERSIONING.md` §\"Scope\" (mirrors 020N conflict-gate.yml posture); no semver bump. Verifies WP-SCP-023 plan-doc invariant 6 (\"Aggregator output is Ed25519-signed\") in spirit — Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub rather than by an SCP-side private key, eliminating the private-key-distribution surface | ACCEPTED | Symmetric posture with D-041 (per-emit data shape + opt-in model) — D-041 ratified the EMITTER side of the trust model; D-042 ratifies the AGGREGATOR / VERIFIER side. The mandatory `--signer-workflow` constraint was already pre-committed at the D-042 reservation note above (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001) — this slice ratifies it as workflow code. The Ed25519-via-Sigstore framing eliminates the chicken-and-egg of \"where does the SCP private key live and how does the aggregator hold it without exposing adopters\" — GitHub manages the keys via OIDC + Sigstore. The two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) is identical to 023B's `policy-check` + `attest-scorecard` split (closes the analogous threat surface where workflow-level write permissions could be exploited by a compromised aggregate-side step). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: aggregator runs on the SCP repo with single-operator identity (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-023 023A plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation + 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure |\n| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B operational contracts for cascade scaffolding (this PR). Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (= `SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically — bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments `--adopter-repo`, `--default-branch`, `--scp-sha`, `--scorecard-emit`, `--output-dir` per plan-doc §5.3. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12; cascade-onboarded adopters standardise on `policy-check-wrapper.yml`, while pre-cascade manual adopters may still have `policy-check.yml` until they rename to the canonical filename (the §12.7.1 callout covers this carve-out and the follow-on `--wrapper-path` work item). (3) `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` mode reverses prior branch-protection mutation from a captured before-state, validates the captured GET-shape JSON, transforms it into the PUT payload by stripping `_links` / `url` / `checks` envelope fields, flattening `enforce_admins.enabled` back to a boolean, preserving `required_pull_request_reviews` recursively, and normalising invalid or absent `restrictions` to null. Restore mode now warns and requires explicit acknowledgements when the captured pre-state would remove `enforce_admins` or clear `required_status_checks.contexts`, captures the observed current branch-protection state immediately before PUT, and mirrors forward-mode's APPLY_FAIL pattern so failed PUTs still emit an audit log before exiting non-zero. New safety check (forward mode only): resolves the canonical wrapper by repo-relative path (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) instead of workflow display name, then refuses to invoke unless the repo has at least one successful `policy-check` workflow run in the last 60 days on the target branch; once a target already has an invocation log entry, forward-mode re-arming requires `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-gate-2>` or the explicit `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` override. (4) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CI enforces invariant 2's 4 cascade-status check behaviours: fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised `cascade-status:`; `onboarded` requires log entry + target match; `onboarded-operator-bump` additionally requires STATUS.md `TF-024X-renovate-<adopter-slug>` row matching regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` requires DISPATCH-NOTE `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference matching regex literally + log file NOT modified. Slug matching canonicalises adopter names to lowercased hyphen-only owner/repo strings so dots/underscores collapse to hyphens before regex matching. Regex (Python re): `TF-024X-(renovate|conflict)-[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)+(?:\\*\\*)? \\((open|pending|in-progress|closed)\\): \\S.{19,}` — matches in STATUS.md or DISPATCH-NOTE; `\\S` anchor at description start prevents all-whitespace bypass; ≥20 chars total. (5) ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure — 3-gate playbook (disable via `--restore` → SHA-pin to last known-good release tag → re-enable after Renovate-bumped fix). All four script components (scaffolder + `--restore` + `--i-understand` flag + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh` covering all four CI behaviours) are hard predecessors for slice 024C. Slice 024B itself ships under documented protocol deviation (direct codex exec / claude -p; non-kernel-dangerous shell + tests + docs scope) per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md` note + justify rule; 024C entry is conditional on `FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001` closure (per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC). | ACCEPTED | D-044 was reserved at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc 024A merge (PR #102, 2026-05-04) per the §9 reservation block; this slice ratifies it. The four-component scope (scaffolder + template + `--restore` + `check-invocation-log-entry.sh`) is the single hardest predecessor surface for cohort cascade — without all four, cascade slices 024C-F would each rebuild the per-adopter wrapper shape, the rollback procedure, and the cascade-status invariant enforcement from scratch (multiplying the 9-round adversarial-review burden that 024A absorbed by 4 cohort slices). The `MANIFEST.json` + SHA256 audit surface mirrors the `install_acc_hook.sh` pattern (atomic config + binary SHA pinning) — provides forensic traceability for cascade-driven adopter-side artefact authorship. The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag closes the cold-start chicken-and-egg: a new adopter has no green CI before the wrapper merges + at least one PR runs, so the safety check would otherwise block first-onboard; the explicit flag is the operator's acknowledgement that they accept the cold-start risk for that single first-onboard run. The break-glass 3-gate procedure is intentionally NOT a one-button kill-switch (all gates auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA-pin is explicit operator consent to step backwards from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures adopters don't stay un-gated forever). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '756,818p' docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md && sed -n '1206,1222p' docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '756,818p' docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md && sed -n '1206,1222p' docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md\"","aggregated_output":"their repo, what to set on their branch protection, what to expect when\nSCP cuts a new release, and how break-glass + rollback work.\n\n#### 12.7.1 Minimal caller wrapper\n\nAdd this file at `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` in your repo. Pin\nthe `uses:` line by 40-character commit SHA, NOT by tag name. The\n`# tag: v1.0.0` comment is the human-readable annotation and the signal\nthe SCP Renovate preset uses to bump the SHA + comment together on every\nSCP release.\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/policy-check.yml\nname: policy-check\n\n\"on\":\n  pull_request:\n    branches: [main]\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  statuses: write  # required for scp/policy-check-readback per D-029 / 020C.1(vi)\n\njobs:\n  policy-check:\n    # Refuse fork PRs — same-repo only for v1.0.0 (mandatory; do not\n    # remove this `if:`. Fork PRs run with the fork's read-only\n    # GITHUB_TOKEN and cannot post the readback commit-status, plus\n    # they can carry malicious workflow-context-injection payloads.\n    # Closes WP-SCP-020 020D1 R1 review TF-D1-002.\n    if: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.event.pull_request.base.repo.full_name }}\n    # renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-\n    uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<commit-SHA>  # tag: v1.0.0\n```\n\nThe `if:` fork-PR refusal is **mandatory**, not optional. Closes the\n20D1 R1 review tracked-forward item TF-D1-002.\n\n**Cascade naming note.** Cascade-onboarded adopters get\n`policy-check-wrapper.yml` (emitted by `scaffold-downstream.sh` per\nWP-SCP-024). Pre-cascade manual adopters using §12.7 may have used\n`policy-check.yml`; cascade rollout via 024C+ standardises on\n`policy-check-wrapper.yml` as the canonical adopter wrapper filename.\nThe forward-mode safety check in `enable-required-check.sh` looks for\nthe canonical path; manual adopters with the older filename should\nrename to the canonical filename before invoking\n`enable-required-check.sh`, or pass\n`--wrapper-path .github/workflows/<their-name>.yml` (TBD: not currently\nimplemented; tracked as TF-024B-003 for follow-on).\n\n**Before deploying:** review §12.7.13 for the v1.0.0 supply-chain posture (OPA + Conftest + Regal SHA256-verified per platform).\n\n**CODEOWNERS for the wrapper.** Multi-maintainer adopters MUST\nprotect this file with CODEOWNERS so a single PR cannot silently\ndelete the fork-PR `if:`, weaken `permissions:`, or change the\npinned SHA without an owning reviewer. Symmetric with §11.10's\nrecommendation for `.scp/rule-config.yaml`. Minimum entry:\n\n```\n.github/workflows/policy-check.yml @your-team-owners\n```\n\n#### 12.7.2 Renovate preset (`extends:` snippet)\n\n1. **Gate 1 (DISABLE):** run `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <captured-pre-state.json>` to restore the target adopter's branch protection from the captured `before` state in the original invocation log entry. The pre-state JSON lives at the bottom of every invocation log block in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; copy it to a local file first before invoking the restore mode.\n   - SLO: `<30 min` from operator decision to restored state once the slice-024B real-repo round-trip evidence exists (`docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md`); until then treat the target as aspirational and verify the round trip before claiming the SLO.\n   - Note: if the captured pre-state would remove `enforce_admins` or clear `required_status_checks.contexts`, the restore exits 2 unless you add `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement` and/or `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`. Those acknowledgements are safe to include unconditionally when the pre-state is known to be degraded.\n2. **Gate 2 (FIX):** pin the adopter wrapper SHA in `policy-check-wrapper.yml` to the release-tag SHA that matches the last known-good tag.\n   Run: `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/ref/tags/<release-tag> --jq .object.sha` to obtain the release-tag SHA. Use this exact SHA as the pin, NOT a main-branch commit SHA.\n   Do NOT pin to an arbitrary main-branch commit SHA - the federation primitive's release-tag protection (per D-030 020J `v*` tag-protection ruleset) is the only audit anchor for known-good versions; a non-tag SHA bypasses that integrity surface.\n3. **Gate 3 (RE-ENABLE):**\n   0. **REQUIRED: pass `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-gate-2>` to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch>` before re-arming.** Do not re-enable without it. If you are intentionally skipping Gate 2 verification for an emergency re-arm, pass `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` instead and record the exception in the invocation log.\n   1. **Verify Gate 2 completion before proceeding:** run\n      `gh api 'repos/<adopter-owner>/<adopter-repo>/contents/.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml' | jq -r .content | base64 -d | grep -E '^[[:space:]]*uses:' | grep '@'`\n      Confirm the SHA-pin matches the release-tag SHA captured in Gate 2 (run `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane-/git/ref/tags/<release-tag> --jq .object.sha` to compare). If the SHA-pin is NOT the release-tag SHA, return to Gate 2 - do NOT re-enable.\n   2. Once the SCP federation primitive ships a fixed release tag (`v1.2.1` or later), Renovate auto-PRs the wrapper SHA bump in the adopter repo. After the Renovate-bump PR merges and the adopter has observed a clean run, re-run `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --repo <owner/repo> --branch <branch>` to re-arm the required check.\n\nThis procedure is intentionally three-step rather than a one-button kill-switch. Every gate is auditable in git history; Gate 2's wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent to step backward from current SCP main; Gate 3 ensures the adopter does not remain permanently un-gated after the defect is fixed. The structure matches the rollback SLO claimed in WP-SCP-024 plan-doc invariant 7: single-operator-doable, <30 min from decision to restored state, and backed by a real restore path rather than a UI-only action.\n\nReference: WP-SCP-024 plan-doc invariant 7; D-044 (slice 024B); D-035 (operator-run + invocation-logged); enable-required-check.sh --restore mode; ADOPT-001 §12.7 federation-primitive adoption.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
